# Every data file lives in data/. Tracked: the building register and its
# schema (the audit trail), and the Estate Office meter workbooks, which are
# committed so the raw data survives a lost laptop. THIS REPOSITORY MUST STAY
# PRIVATE - those workbooks are the Institute's data, not ours to publish.
# Everything else in data/ is reproducible from a download and stays out.
data/*
!data/README.md
!data/building_register.csv
!data/register_schema.yml
!data/*.xlsm
!data/*.xlsx
!data/candidate_shortlist.csv
# OSM is a living map: this extract is a dated snapshot and re-downloading it
# later would not reproduce the same footprints, so it is tracked.
!data/footprints_osm.json
# PVGIS horizon profile: small, and it pins a regression test.
!data/horizon_*.json
# Part 4 working layers: small, hand-edited, and the roof outlines are the
# project's primary measurement - they must be versioned.
!data/candidate_roofs.geojson
!data/obstructions_template.geojson
!data/roofs.gpkg
!data/obstructions.gpkg
# NASA POWER and PVGIS for a fixed date range are deterministic re-downloads,
# so they stay out - see data/README.md.

# Large spatial outputs
*.tif
*.tiff
*.laz
*.las
*.shp
*.shx
*.dbf
*.prj
*.cpg

# The Part 4 working layers are tracked (allowlisted in the data block
# above). Any OTHER GeoPackage is a derived product and stays out.
data/*.gpkg-shm
data/*.gpkg-wal

# QGIS
*.qgz~
*.qgs~
.qgis2/
qgis/*.gpkg-shm
qgis/*.gpkg-wal

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.ruff_cache/

# OpenDSS run output
*.dss_out
scripts/opendss_out/

# macOS
.DS_Store
